  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HEROES: Child Health Care RBF</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Maternal, Newborn and Child Health (MNCH) indicators have remained low in selected districts in Eastern Uganda (need for statistics).  

Thus the contracted health facilities will use the additional funding as per RBF policies and practices and invest/spend at least 60% of the funds received on quality-of-care improvement that is in line with the facility business plans that will benefit antenatal and newborn care</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To strengthen health systems of 15 selected health facilities to provide better quality of care services for prenatal and newborn in Eastern Uganda. 

 

Specific Objectives 

Increased access to quality safe births in Cordaid supported districts in Eastern Uganda  

Ensure that the newborns are fully immunized by 12 months 

Enhance prenatal care for pregnant mothers with a view of enabling newborn babies to reach their first anniversary in good health  

Promote right nutrition for children aged 0-12 months</narrative>
  </description>
